  "notes": [
   "Step 1 parts were correct; no parts added or dropped.",
   "Peripheral (nano1): GND goes by wire1 to the breadboard top ground rail (tn). Wire2 runs from the rail to column 10 on the top half, which is the button's side 1. Wire3 runs from D2 to column 8 on the bottom half, which is the button's side 2. Pressing the button joins D2 to GND. The sketch uses INPUT_PULLUP, so no resistor is needed.",
   "The button straddles the centre gap in columns 8 and 10 with its legs on rows f (top) and e (bottom). The column numbers are read from the picture, so they are approximate.",
   "The exact rail hole numbers (tn.1 and tn.8) and the wire rows (10t.g, 8b.d) are read from the picture, so they are approximate. They sit in the right strips.",
   "The central board (nano2) has only a USB cable and no extra circuit. It uses its onboard RGB LED.",
   "The USB cable has no ports in the catalogue, so its edges are joined only, with no port on the cable side."
  ]
 },
